<title>PERU: Peru's Luz del Sur sets cash dividend.</title>
<headline>Peru's Luz del Sur sets cash dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peruvian electricity distributor Luz del Sur agreed a cash dividend of 0.052 soles per share with a record date of October 22 and a payout date of October 29, according to a Lima Stock Exchange report Friday.</p>
<p>The dividend is based on profits this year.</p>
<p>Luz del Sur, formerly known as Edelsur, was privatized in 1994 when a consortium consisting of Chilean company Chilquinta International Inc. and Canada's Ontario Hydro Inc paid $212.1 million for a 60 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
